course: dictionary
lesson: 9986
title: Technical words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Technical is an adjective that tells you something is to do with science, machines, computers or a practical skill. «The computer had a technical problem, so the lesson was moved.» The clues are computer and problem: technical means a problem that needs special knowledge to fix.
explain: Technical words are special words that experts use in their subject, such as «denominator» in maths or «photosynthesis» in science. You may not know them yet, but the sentence around them often shows they are important names for something. Ask yourself: is this a special word that only experts would use?
explain: Technical can also mean following the exact rules strictly. «He was given a technical foul, even though nobody was hurt.» Here technical is not about machines at all. Always check which meaning fits the sentence by swapping in your meaning and reading it again.
fact: Technical means to do with science, machines, computers or practical skills.
fact: Technical words are special words used by experts in a subject, such as «photosynthesis».
fact: «Technical» can also mean following the exact rules strictly, as in «a technical foul».
fact: Phrases you will meet are technical problem, technical terms, technical support and technical skill.
fact: «Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious» is a made-up word meaning wonderful, and many of the longest dictionary words are technical ones.
exercise: «The computer had a technical problem, so the lesson was moved.» What does technical describe here? | Very slow and quiet | To do with singing songs | *To do with computers and machines | To do with cooking food
exercise: «The scientist used the word photosynthesis to explain how plants make food.» Find and copy one technical word. | *photosynthesis | plants | explained | scientist
exercise: Asha says, «It was a technical foul, even though nobody got hurt.» What does technical mean here? | *Following the exact rules strictly | Made of wood and paper | Full of bright flowers | Very old and worn
test: What is a technical term? | A word for a happy feeling | A word that means very quiet | *A special word used by experts in a subject | A word that rhymes with a famous film
test: Why are many of the longest dictionary words technical ones? | Long words are always made up for films | *Experts need exact, specialised names for things in their subject | Technical words are shorter than other words | Experts never use long words
exam: Which sentence uses technical to mean following the exact rules? | «The robot has a technical fault in its arm.» | *«He was given a technical foul for holding the player.» | «The technical words were hard to learn.» | «The technical drawing shows the new bridge.»
